{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792611707,"nonce":"drEXgqwpF9jA4xT6i3DkXt+TmoI=","title":"TypeScript: expose compatible checker options including relaxed opt-in modes","message":"Official cases explicitly selecting strict=false, noImplicitAny=false or strictNullChecks=false are skipped because native Options currently exposes soundness only. Other checker flags also need deliberate semantics rather than being sent only to the oracle.\n\nKeep strict static checking the default. Offer explicit opt-in compatibility modes for users; do not turn the initial static implementation into a fixed deliberate language limitation. Separate checker choices (nullability, implicit-any, unused checks, exact optional properties) from runtime representation/capability needs. Include project/CLI plumbing and cache-key invalidation for options affecting checked artifacts.\n\nThe official-corpus driver must keep unsupported option combinations as visible skips until the native checker honors them. Corpus adapter/CI limitations remain 63f459c5d2cf4b513599a90423637eee9adf5faa296254a5e4cb139c152eeb87.\n\nEvidence: official TypeScript conformance corpus at 3e9236361fa97a9e6c685f4833ac457ae2d8c50a, oracle 7.1.0-beta, native d978fe3fa5f8f7480d0c0d1b7dd2ca4548b490f0. This is check-only acceptance/category comparison under strict defaults, not JIT/runtime coverage. The full affected-case inventory will be attached after the complete audited run. Parent: 6875fc2949f83d682861ecab814e0ff82c824f5990620b0d64ca0340ebb026e5.","files":null}]}